course: dictionary
lesson: 12407
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can mean different things. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The Cyclops had one huge eye in the middle of his forehead.» Giant and forehead tell you this is a giant from an old story.
explain: «Under the microscope, Mia spotted a cyclops swimming in the pond water.» Microscope and pond are the clues, so cyclops here is a tiny animal, not a giant. Always ask: which meaning fits these clues?
explain: «The cyclops in the film shot beams of light from his eyes.» Film and beams tell you cyclops is a name for a hero in comics and films. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well.
fact: A Cyclops, in myths, is a giant with only one eye in the middle of its forehead.
fact: The most famous Cyclops is Polyphemus, who trapped Odysseus (Ulysses) in his cave.
fact: In science, a cyclops is a tiny freshwater animal, a kind of crustacean, with one eye spot. You can find one in a pond.
fact: The plural can be cyclopes, cyclopses or cyclops.
fact: Cyclops is also a character name in comics and films, such as the X-Men hero who shoots beams from his eyes.
exercise: «The Cyclops in the cave had only one eye.» What is a Cyclops in this sentence? | A hero who shoots beams from his eyes | A tiny animal in a pond | A cave on a Greek island | *A giant with one eye in the middle of its forehead
exercise: «Under the microscope we saw a cyclops with one dark eye spot.» What is the cyclops here? | A giant from a Greek story | A superhero in a film | A king who lived in a cave | *A tiny freshwater animal found in ponds
exercise: «The cyclops Polyphemus trapped Odysseus in his cave.» Who did Polyphemus trap? | Nobody | *Odysseus | A copepod | The X-Men
test: «The X-Men hero Cyclops shot beams from his eyes.» What does cyclops mean here? | *A character name for a hero in comics and films | A one-eyed giant from myth | A cave on a Greek island | A tiny pond animal
test: Which is a correct plural of cyclops? | Cyclop | *Cyclopes | Cyclopis | Cyclopy
exam: Mia reads «Mia spotted a cyclops swimming in the pond under her magnifying glass.» What does cyclops mean here? | A giant with one eye | A hero in a film | *A tiny freshwater animal | A Greek king
